hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1495","Saad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakim bin Ayan told us strange news. My father told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Yaqoub, on the authority of Qais bin Rafi’ al-Qaisi, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that Abdullah bin Amr passed With Muadh bin Jabal, and he was standing at his door, gesturing with his hand, as if he was talking to himself, and Abdullah said to him: What is the matter with you, Abu Abdul? The Most Gracious, are you talking to yourself? He said: Why would the enemy of God want to distract me from words I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Are you now toiling in your home? Go out to the assembly and speak, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever strives in the cause of God is a guarantor of God. Whoever visits a sick person is responsible for God, and whoever goes to the mosque tomorrow or goes is responsible for God, and whoever visits an imam whom he visits is responsible for God, and whoever sits in his house and does not backbite anyone in any wrongful way, he is responsible for God.” The enemy of God wants to expel me from my house to the assembly."
